# Browser
# Companion in the browser (CR 103.2b, 702.139a, 116.2g). Both players chose Lurrus of the Dream-Den as their companion when
# they built their decks, and both decks fulfil its condition, so both are revealed before the game with nothing asked. Bot1's
# page shows its own in a Companion window at the bottom left of its battlefield, and Bot2's at the top left of Bot2's; neither
# is in a sideboard button of Bot2's rail. With Black Lotus out, Bot1 clicks its Lurrus, which offers "{3}: Put Lurrus of the
# Dream-Den in hand.", takes it paying with the Lotus, and its window is gone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Swamp x19

[Bot1 Sideboard]
Lightning Bolt

[Bot1 Companion]
Lurrus of the Dream-Den

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot2 Sideboard]
Counterspell

[Bot2 Companion]
Lurrus of the Dream-Den

[Actions]
? Client.Bot1.Companion = Lurrus of the Dream-Den
? Client.Bot1.Companion.Corner = bottom-left
? Client.Bot1.OpponentCompanion = Lurrus of the Dream-Den
? Client.Bot1.OpponentCompanion.Corner = top-left
? Client.Bot1.OpponentSideboard.Caption =
? Client.Bot1.Sideboard.Caption = Sideboard  2
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Sideboard.Lurrus of the Dream-Den.TakeCompanion
? Client.Bot1.Menu = {3}: Put Lurrus of the Dream-Den in hand.
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
? Client.Bot1.Hand = Swamp; Swamp; Swamp; Swamp; Swamp; Swamp; Lurrus of the Dream-Den
? Client.Bot1.Companion =
? Client.Bot1.OpponentCompanion = Lurrus of the Dream-Den
? Client.Bot1.Sideboard.Caption = Sideboard  1
? Client.Bot1.Log.Has = You put [Lurrus of the Dream-Den] into your hand from outside the game.
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Companion = Lurrus of the Dream-Den
Bot1.Sideboard = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Companion = Lurrus of the Dream-Den
Bot2.Sideboard = Counterspell; Lurrus of the Dream-Den
